    <!-- An Android TV's developer connection (network ADB), beside the remote: the TV's own inputs and apps, and its brightness on some sets -->
    <string name="dev_link_title">Developer connection</string>
    <string name="dev_link_body">Lists the TV\'s own inputs and all its apps, switches inputs on TVs that ignore the HDMI keys, and sets the brightness on some. It goes over the TV\'s debugging connection (ADB). Keys and typing work the same without it.</string>
    <string name="dev_link_step_developer">On the TV, open Settings › System › About and select Android TV OS build seven times. On older TVs it\'s Device Preferences › About › Build.</string>
    <string name="dev_link_step_debugging">Open Developer options, next to About, and turn on USB debugging. On a Shield it\'s Network debugging.</string>
    <string name="dev_link_step_allow">Tap Connect, then on the TV tick Always allow and choose OK.</string>
    <string name="dev_link_connect">Connect</string>
    <string name="dev_link_allow">Allow on the TV</string>
    <string name="dev_link_allow_body">Tick Always allow from this computer, then OK</string>
    <string name="dev_link_turn_off">Turn off</string>
    <string name="dev_link_off">Off. Adds inputs and all apps</string>
    <string name="dev_link_away">The TV isn\'t answering. It tries again by itself while the remote is open.</string>
    <string name="dev_link_away_short">Not answering</string>
    <string name="dev_link_debugging_off">The TV turned it away. Check that USB debugging is on. Since Android TV 14 some TVs only take Wireless debugging, which TennaRC can\'t use yet.</string>
    <string name="dev_link_debugging_off_short">Debugging is off on the TV</string>
    <string name="dev_link_wireless">Only Wireless debugging is on, which TennaRC can\'t use yet. Turn on USB debugging too, or pair from a computer once and run adb tcpip 5555, which lasts until the TV restarts.</string>
    <string name="dev_link_wireless_short">Only Wireless debugging is on</string>
    <string name="dev_link_not_allowed">Nobody allowed it on the TV. Try again, and choose OK there.</string>
    <string name="dev_link_not_allowed_short">Not allowed on the TV</string>
    <string name="dev_link_forgotten">The TV has forgotten this phone, as Android TV does with one it hasn\'t seen for a week. Try again, and allow it on the TV.</string>
    <string name="dev_link_forgotten_short">The TV forgot this phone</string>
